STORIES_LOAD("lk",{"lk1":{"passage":[[1,5,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"Zechariah was an old priest, and his wife Elizabeth was descended from Aaron. They both loved and obeyed God. But they had no children, and they were both very old."},{"sc":"temple","n":"One day, Zechariah was chosen by lot to go into the temple and burn incense. A once-in-a-lifetime honour! Outside, all the people were praying."},{"sc":"temple","n":"Suddenly an angel appeared, standing at the right side of the altar of incense! Zechariah was terrified. \"Don't be afraid, Zechariah. Your prayer has been heard! Your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you are to call him John. He will go before the Lord in the spirit and power of Elijah.\""},{"sc":"temple","w":"bzechlk","e":"worried","t":"How can I be sure of this? I'm an old man, and my wife is well along in years!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"\"I am Gabriel. I stand in the presence of God, and I've been sent to tell you this good news. Because you didn't believe my words, you'll be silent and unable to speak until the day this happens.\""},{"sc":"temple","n":"When Zechariah came out, he couldn't speak, only make signs. The people realised he had seen a vision. And soon, just as Gabriel said, Elizabeth was expecting a baby!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"📜 Promise kept: Malachi, the last prophet, promised that God would send 'Elijah' before the day of the Lord (Malachi 4:5-6). After 400 years of silence, Gabriel announced the baby who would fulfil it: John the Baptist!"}],"lesson":{"title":"God hears long prayers","text":"Zechariah and Elizabeth had prayed for a child for years, maybe decades. They had probably given up. But God had heard every prayer. Keep praying, even when the answer seems slow. And when God speaks, believe Him."},"order":["Zechariah and Elizabeth are old and childless","Zechariah burns incense in the temple","The angel Gabriel appears","\"Your wife will have a son\"","Zechariah doubts","He can't speak until the baby is born"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who appeared to Zechariah in the temple?","o":["The angel Gabriel","Elijah","Moses","Michael"],"why":"Luke 1:19."},{"q":"What happened because Zechariah doubted?","o":["He couldn't speak","He went blind","He fell asleep","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 1:20."},{"q":"What were they told to name the baby?","o":["John","Zechariah","Jesus","Elijah"],"why":"Luke 1:13."}],"words":["GABRIEL","TEMPLE","INCENSE","PRAYER","JOHN","SILENT"]},"lk2":{"passage":[[1,26,38]],"intro":[{"sc":"hut","n":"Six months later, God sent the angel Gabriel to Nazareth, a small town in Galilee, to a young woman named Mary. She was engaged to Joseph, a descendant of David."},{"sc":"hut","n":"\"Greetings, you who are highly favoured! The Lord is with you.\" Mary was very troubled and wondered what kind of greeting this was."},{"sc":"hut","n":"\"Don't be afraid, Mary; you have found favour with God. You will conceive and give birth to a son, and you are to call Him Jesus. He will be great and will be called the Son of the Most High. The Lord God will give Him the throne of His father David, and His kingdom will never end.\""},{"sc":"hut","w":"bmary","e":"worried","t":"How will this be, since I am a virgin?"},{"sc":"hut","n":"\"The Holy Spirit will come on you, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you. So the holy one to be born will be called the Son of God. Even your relative Elizabeth is going to have a child in her old age. For no word from God will ever fail.\""},{"sc":"hut","w":"bmary","e":"smile","t":"I am the Lord's servant. May it be to me as you have said."},{"sc":"hut","n":"📜 Promise kept: Isaiah 7:14 promised a virgin would give birth to a son, and 2 Samuel 7 promised David a King whose kingdom would last for ever. Gabriel announced that both were coming true, in Mary's baby."}],"lesson":{"title":"Say yes to God","text":"Mary was young, and this news would turn her life upside down. She asked an honest question: 'How?' Then she said the bravest yes in history: 'I am the Lord's servant.' Leaders ask honest questions, and then say yes to God, trusting Him with the rest."},"order":["Gabriel visits Mary in Nazareth","\"The Lord is with you\"","\"You will give birth to a son, Jesus\"","\"How will this be?\"","\"The Holy Spirit will come on you\"","\"I am the Lord's servant\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Mary live?","o":["Nazareth","Bethlehem","Jerusalem","Egypt"],"why":"Luke 1:26-27."},{"q":"What did Gabriel say Jesus would be called?","o":["The Son of the Most High","A prophet","A carpenter","A priest"],"why":"Luke 1:32."},{"q":"What was Mary's answer?","o":["\"I am the Lord's servant\"","\"No thank you\"","\"Ask someone else\"","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 1:38."}],"words":["MARY","GABRIEL","SERVANT","FAVOUR","NAZARETH","SON"]},"lk3":{"passage":[[1,39,55]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Mary hurried to a town in the hill country of Judea to visit her relative Elizabeth."},{"sc":"hut","n":"When Elizabeth heard Mary's greeting, the baby inside her LEAPT! And Elizabeth was filled with the Holy Spirit."},{"sc":"hut","w":"belizabeth","e":"big","t":"Blessed are you among women, and blessed is the child you will bear! Why am I so favoured, that the mother of my Lord should come to me? As soon as I heard your greeting, the baby in my womb leapt for joy!"},{"sc":"hut","w":"bmary","e":"big","t":"My soul glorifies the Lord, and my spirit rejoices in God my Saviour, for He has been mindful of the humble state of His servant!"},{"sc":"hut","n":"\"He has brought down rulers from their thrones but has lifted up the humble. He has filled the hungry with good things but has sent the rich away empty.\""},{"sc":"hut","n":"Mary stayed with Elizabeth for about three months, then went home."},{"sc":"hut","n":"🔎 Did you know? Mary's song is called the 'Magnificat', from its first word in Latin. It's full of echoes of Hannah's song in 1 Samuel 2. Mary knew her Scriptures well! Churches have sung it every evening for over a thousand years."}],"lesson":{"title":"Celebrate together","text":"Two women, one old and one young, both carrying miracle babies, celebrated together. Even unborn John leapt for joy! Then Mary sang about a God who lifts up the humble and fills the hungry. Leaders celebrate what God is doing in others, and remember that God turns the world's order upside down."},"order":["Mary visits Elizabeth","Elizabeth's baby leaps for joy","Elizabeth is filled with the Spirit","\"Blessed are you among women\"","Mary sings, \"My soul glorifies the Lord\"","God lifts up the humble"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Elizabeth's baby do when Mary arrived?","o":["Leapt for joy","Cried","Slept","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 1:44."},{"q":"What is Mary's song called?","o":["The Magnificat","The Psalm","The Hallel","The Beatitudes"],"why":"From its first Latin word."},{"q":"Whose song from the Old Testament does Mary's song echo?","o":["Hannah's","Miriam's","Deborah's","Ruth's"],"why":"1 Samuel 2."}],"words":["LEAPT","JOY","ELIZABETH","MAGNIFICAT","HUMBLE","SONG"]},"lk4":{"passage":[[1,57,66],[1,76,79]],"intro":[{"sc":"hut","n":"When it was time, Elizabeth gave birth to a son. Her neighbours and relatives heard how the Lord had shown her great mercy, and they shared her joy."},{"sc":"hut","n":"On the eighth day, they came to name the child. They were going to call him Zechariah, after his father. But Elizabeth said, \"No! He is to be called John.\""},{"sc":"hut","n":"\"But no one in your family has that name!\" They made signs to his father to ask what he'd like to name him."},{"sc":"hut","n":"Zechariah asked for a writing tablet, and to everyone's astonishment, he wrote: \"His name is John.\""},{"sc":"hut","w":"bzechlk","e":"big","t":"Praise be to the Lord, the God of Israel, because He has come to His people and redeemed them!"},{"sc":"hut","n":"Immediately his mouth was opened and his tongue set free, and he began to speak, praising God! After nine months of silence, he sang about his tiny son: \"You, my child, will be called a prophet of the Most High, for you will go before the Lord to prepare the way for Him... to shine on those living in darkness.\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Obedience opens your mouth","text":"Zechariah had doubted Gabriel. But nine months of silence taught him trust. When he obeyed and wrote 'His name is John', his voice came back, and the first thing he did was praise God. Leaders learn from their mistakes, and use their voice to praise God."},"order":["Elizabeth gives birth to a son","Relatives want to call him Zechariah","Elizabeth says, \"He is John\"","Zechariah writes, \"His name is John\"","His voice comes back","He praises God and prophesies"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the relatives want to name the baby?","o":["Zechariah","John","Jesus","David"],"why":"Luke 1:59."},{"q":"How did Zechariah tell them the name?","o":["He wrote it on a tablet","He shouted","He sang","He pointed"],"why":"Luke 1:63."},{"q":"What happened when he wrote it?","o":["He could speak again","He fell asleep","Nothing","He left"],"why":"Luke 1:64."}],"words":["JOHN","NAME","TABLET","PRAISE","VOICE","PROPHET"]},"lk5":{"passage":[[2,1,7]],"intro":[{"sc":"persia","n":"In those days, Caesar Augustus, the emperor in faraway Rome, ordered a census of the whole Roman world. Everyone had to go to their family's home town to be registered."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"So Joseph went up from Nazareth in Galilee to Bethlehem in Judea, the town of David, because he belonged to David's family. Mary, who was expecting a baby, went with him: a journey of about 150 kilometres!"},{"sc":"bethlehem","n":"While they were there, the time came for the baby to be born."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"Mary gave birth to her firstborn, a son. She wrapped Him in strips of cloth and placed Him in a manger, an animals' feeding trough, because there was no guest room available for them."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"📜 Promise kept: Micah had promised the Ruler would come from Bethlehem (Micah 5:2). Mary and Joseph lived in Nazareth, 150 km away! God used a pagan emperor's census to get them to exactly the right town at exactly the right time."},{"sc":"nativity","n":"🔎 Did you know? The 'inn' was probably the guest room of a family house. Many homes had animals sleeping on the ground floor at night, with a manger cut into the floor. The King of the universe was born where the animals ate."}],"lesson":{"title":"God came low","text":"The Son of God wasn't born in a palace, but laid in an animals' feeding trough, because there was no room. God came to the lowest place, so that no one would be too low for Him. Leaders make room for Jesus, and don't despise humble beginnings."},"order":["Caesar orders a census","Joseph and Mary travel to Bethlehem","It's about 150 km","The baby is born","Mary wraps Him in cloths","She lays Him in a manger"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who ordered the census?","o":["Caesar Augustus","King Herod","Pilate","Nebuchadnezzar"],"why":"Luke 2:1."},{"q":"Where was baby Jesus laid?","o":["In a manger","In a cradle","In a palace","In a boat"],"why":"Luke 2:7."},{"q":"Why was He laid there?","o":["There was no guest room for them","It was warm","Mary liked it","It was the custom"],"why":"Luke 2:7."}],"words":["MANGER","CENSUS","BETHLEHEM","ROOM","CLOTHS","BORN"]},"lk6":{"passage":[[2,8,20]],"intro":[{"sc":"shepherdsnight","n":"There were shepherds living out in the fields nearby, keeping watch over their flocks at night. Shepherds were poor, smelly, and not trusted by many people."},{"sc":"shepherdsnight","n":"Suddenly an angel of the Lord appeared to them, and the glory of the Lord shone around them. They were terrified!"},{"sc":"shepherdsnight","n":"\"Don't be afraid! I bring you good news that will cause great joy for all the people. Today in the town of David a Saviour has been born to you; He is the Messiah, the Lord. This will be a sign to you: you will find a baby wrapped in cloths and lying in a manger.\""},{"sc":"shepherdsnight","n":"Suddenly a great company of the heavenly host appeared with the angel, praising God: \"Glory to God in the highest heaven, and on earth peace to those on whom His favour rests!\""},{"sc":"shepherdsnight","w":"bshepherd","e":"big","t":"Let's go to Bethlehem and see this thing that has happened!"},{"sc":"nativity","n":"They hurried off and found Mary and Joseph, and the baby lying in the manger, just as they'd been told. Then they spread the word everywhere! And Mary treasured up all these things and pondered them in her heart."}],"lesson":{"title":"Good news for ordinary people","text":"God didn't announce Jesus' birth to kings or priests first, but to night-shift shepherds that others looked down on. And they didn't keep it quiet: they hurried, saw, and told everyone. The good news is for everyone. Leaders hurry to Jesus, and then share what they've seen."},"order":["Shepherds watch their flocks at night","An angel appears","\"Good news of great joy\"","\"A Saviour has been born\"","Many angels praise God","The shepherds hurry and find the baby"],"quiz":[{"q":"What sign did the angel give?","o":["A baby wrapped in cloths, lying in a manger","A star","A crown","A rainbow"],"why":"Luke 2:12."},{"q":"What did the angels sing?","o":["Glory to God in the highest","Hosanna","Holy, holy, holy","Amen"],"why":"Luke 2:14."},{"q":"What did Mary do with all these things?","o":["Treasured them in her heart","Forgot them","Wrote a book","Told no one"],"why":"Luke 2:19."}],"words":["SHEPHERDS","ANGELS","GLORY","SAVIOUR","MANGER","GOODNEWS"]},"lk7":{"passage":[[2,25,38]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"When Jesus was forty days old, Mary and Joseph took Him to the temple in Jerusalem to present Him to the Lord. They offered a pair of doves, the offering of poor families."},{"sc":"temple","n":"In Jerusalem lived an old man named Simeon, righteous and devout. The Holy Spirit had told him he wouldn't die before he had seen the Lord's Messiah. Moved by the Spirit, he went into the temple courts that very day."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bsimeon","e":"big","t":"Sovereign Lord, as You have promised, You may now let Your servant go in peace. For my eyes have seen Your salvation, a light for revelation to the nations, and the glory of Your people Israel!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"Simeon took the baby in his arms. Then he told Mary, gently: \"A sword will pierce your own soul too.\" One day, she would watch her Son suffer."},{"sc":"temple","n":"There was also a prophetess, Anna, 84 years old. She had been a widow for most of her life, and she never left the temple: she worshipped night and day, fasting and praying."},{"sc":"temple","w":"banna","e":"big","t":"Thank You, Lord! This is the One we've been waiting for!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"Anna came up at that very moment, gave thanks to God, and spoke about the child to everyone who was looking forward to the redemption of Jerusalem."}],"lesson":{"title":"Faithful waiting is rewarded","text":"Simeon and Anna had waited and prayed their whole lives. They were old, and nobody important. But they were the first to recognise the baby Messiah in the temple, because they were close to God. Leaders stay faithful in prayer over many years, and respect the wisdom of the elderly."},"order":["Mary and Joseph bring Jesus to the temple","They offer two doves","Simeon takes Jesus in his arms","\"My eyes have seen Your salvation\"","Anna, aged 84, gives thanks","She tells everyone about the child"],"quiz":[{"q":"What had the Holy Spirit promised Simeon?","o":["He'd see the Messiah before he died","He'd be rich","He'd be king","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 2:26."},{"q":"How old was Anna?","o":["84","12","40","100"],"why":"Luke 2:37."},{"q":"What did Simeon call Jesus?","o":["A light for the nations","A king of Rome","A teacher","A soldier"],"why":"Luke 2:32."}],"words":["SIMEON","ANNA","TEMPLE","SALVATION","LIGHT","WAITED"]},"lk8":{"passage":[[2,41,52]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"Every year Jesus' parents went to Jerusalem for the Passover festival. When Jesus was twelve years old, they went up as usual."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"After the festival, His parents set off for home with a big group of relatives and friends. They thought Jesus was somewhere in the crowd. After a whole day's walk, they started looking for Him, and couldn't find Him anywhere!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"They hurried back to Jerusalem. For three days they searched!"},{"sc":"temple","n":"At last they found Him in the temple courts, sitting among the teachers, listening to them and asking them questions. Everyone was amazed at His understanding and His answers."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bmary","e":"worried","t":"Son, why have You treated us like this? Your father and I have been anxiously searching for You!"},{"sc":"temple","w":"byoungjesus","e":"smile","t":"Why were you searching for Me? Didn't you know I had to be in My Father's house?"},{"sc":"hut","n":"Then He went down to Nazareth with them and was obedient to them. And Jesus grew in wisdom and stature, and in favour with God and people."}],"lesson":{"title":"Grow in four ways","text":"At twelve, Jesus loved God's house and asked great questions. Then He went home and obeyed His parents. Luke says He grew in four ways: wisdom (mind), stature (body), favour with God (spirit), and favour with people (friendships). Leaders grow in all four ways too."},"order":["Jesus goes to Passover at twelve","His parents start home without Him","They search for three days","They find Him in the temple","\"I had to be in My Father's house\"","He grows in wisdom and stature"],"quiz":[{"q":"How old was Jesus in this story?","o":["Twelve","Five","Thirty","Eighteen"],"why":"Luke 2:42."},{"q":"Where did they find Him?","o":["In the temple, with the teachers","At the market","At home","By the lake"],"why":"Luke 2:46."},{"q":"In what four ways did Jesus grow?","o":["Wisdom, stature, favour with God and people","Height, weight, age and money","Running, swimming, reading, writing","None"],"why":"Luke 2:52."}],"words":["TWELVE","TEMPLE","TEACHERS","WISDOM","STATURE","FATHER"]},"lk9":{"passage":[[4,16,30]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Jesus went to Nazareth, where He had grown up, and on the Sabbath He went into the synagogue, as He usually did."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"He stood up to read, and the scroll of the prophet Isaiah was handed to Him. He unrolled it and found the place where it is written:"},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"The Spirit of the Lord is on Me, because He has anointed Me to proclaim good news to the poor. He has sent Me to proclaim freedom for the prisoners and recovery of sight for the blind, to set the oppressed free, to proclaim the year of the Lord's favour."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"He rolled up the scroll, gave it back to the attendant and sat down. The eyes of everyone in the synagogue were fastened on Him."},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Today this Scripture is fulfilled in your hearing."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"At first they were impressed. But when Jesus reminded them that God had once helped a foreign widow in Zarephath and a foreign general named Naaman, they became furious! They drove Him out of town to the edge of a cliff to throw Him off. But He walked right through the crowd and went on His way."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"📜 Promise kept: Remember Isaiah 61? Jesus chose it as His 'mission statement'. And remember the widow of Zarephath and Naaman from 1 and 2 Kings? Jesus used them to show God's love was always meant for foreigners too."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus' mission: good news for the poor","text":"Jesus chose Isaiah 61 as His mission: good news for the poor, freedom for prisoners, sight for the blind, freedom for the oppressed. And He reminded His home town that God's love includes outsiders. Leaders who follow Jesus share His mission."},"order":["Jesus goes to the synagogue in Nazareth","He reads from Isaiah","\"Good news to the poor\"","\"Today this Scripture is fulfilled\"","He mentions the widow of Zarephath and Naaman","The crowd tries to throw Him off a cliff"],"quiz":[{"q":"Which prophet's scroll did Jesus read?","o":["Isaiah","Jeremiah","Daniel","Malachi"],"why":"Luke 4:17."},{"q":"What did Jesus say after reading?","o":["Today this Scripture is fulfilled","Isaiah was wrong","Maybe one day","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 4:21."},{"q":"Which two foreigners did Jesus mention?","o":["The widow of Zarephath and Naaman","Pharaoh and Goliath","Ruth and Rahab","Cyrus and Darius"],"why":"Luke 4:25-27."}],"words":["NAZARETH","SCROLL","ISAIAH","FULFILLED","POOR","FREEDOM"]},"lk10":{"passage":[[5,1,11]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"One day Jesus was standing by the Lake of Gennesaret (Galilee), with crowds pressing around Him. He saw two boats at the water's edge, left by fishermen who were washing their nets."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"He got into Simon Peter's boat and asked him to push out a little. Then He sat down and taught the people from the boat."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Put out into deep water, and let down the nets for a catch."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bpeter","e":"worried","t":"Master, we've worked hard all night and haven't caught anything. But because You say so, I will let down the nets."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"When they did, they caught such a large number of fish that their nets began to break! They called their partners in the other boat, and they filled both boats so full that they began to sink!"},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bpeter","e":"worried","t":"Go away from me, Lord; I am a sinful man!"},{"sc":"galilee","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't be afraid; from now on you will fish for people."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"So they pulled their boats up on shore, left everything and followed Him."}],"lesson":{"title":"Because You say so","text":"Peter was the expert fisherman, and Jesus was a carpenter. Peter knew you don't catch fish in daytime in deep water! But he obeyed anyway: 'because You say so'. When Jesus' power showed, Peter felt unworthy, but Jesus called him anyway. Leaders obey Jesus even when it doesn't make sense to them."},"order":["Jesus teaches from Peter's boat","\"Put out into deep water\"","\"We worked all night and caught nothing\"","\"Because You say so\"","The nets begin to break","They leave everything and follow"],"quiz":[{"q":"How long had Peter fished without catching anything?","o":["All night","One hour","A week","A month"],"why":"Luke 5:5."},{"q":"What happened to the nets?","o":["They began to break","They were empty","They were lost","They caught fire"],"why":"Luke 5:6."},{"q":"What did Peter say when he saw the catch?","o":["Go away from me, I'm a sinful man","Let's sell them!","Thank You!","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 5:8."}],"words":["NETS","FISH","DEEP","OBEY","BOATS","SINFUL"]},"lk11":{"passage":[[7,11,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"citygate","n":"Jesus went to a town called Nain, with His disciples and a large crowd."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"As He approached the town gate, a funeral procession was coming out. The dead man was the only son of his mother, and she was a widow. A large crowd from the town was with her."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Without a husband or a son, a widow in those days had no one to provide for her. She had lost everything."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"When the Lord saw her, His heart went out to her."},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Don't cry."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"Then He went up and touched the bier they were carrying him on, and the bearers stood still."},{"sc":"citygate","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"Young man, I say to you, get up!"},{"sc":"citygate","n":"The dead man sat up and began to talk, and Jesus gave him back to his mother. They were all filled with awe and praised God: \"A great prophet has appeared among us! God has come to help His people!\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus' heart goes out to the hurting","text":"Nobody asked Jesus for help. He saw a grieving widow, His heart went out to her, and He acted. Notice His first words: 'Don't cry.' Then He gave her son back to her. Leaders notice people who are hurting, even when they don't ask for help."},"order":["Jesus goes to Nain","A funeral comes out of the gate","The dead man is a widow's only son","Jesus' heart goes out to her","\"Young man, get up!\"","Jesus gives him back to his mother"],"quiz":[{"q":"Who had died?","o":["A widow's only son","A king","A soldier","A priest"],"why":"Luke 7:12."},{"q":"What did Jesus say to the mother first?","o":["Don't cry","Go home","Who is this?","Pray"],"why":"Luke 7:13."},{"q":"What did the people say?","o":["God has come to help His people","That's impossible","Go away","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 7:16."}],"words":["NAIN","WIDOW","SON","COMPASSION","GETUP","MOTHER"]},"lk12":{"passage":[[7,36,50]],"intro":[{"sc":"banquet","n":"A Pharisee named Simon invited Jesus to dinner. Guests reclined at a low table, lying on their sides with their feet behind them."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"A woman who had lived a sinful life in that town heard Jesus was there. She came with an alabaster jar of perfume. She stood behind Him at His feet, weeping, and her tears wet His feet. She wiped them with her hair, kissed them, and poured perfume on them."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bsimonph","e":"frown","t":"(thinking) If this man were a prophet, He would know what kind of woman is touching Him!"},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Simon, two people owed money to a moneylender. One owed 500 coins, the other 50. Neither could pay, so he forgave both debts. Which of them will love him more?"},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bsimonph","e":"smile","t":"The one who had the bigger debt forgiven, I suppose."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"You didn't give Me water for My feet, but she wet them with her tears. You didn't give Me a kiss, but she hasn't stopped kissing My feet. Her many sins have been forgiven, as her great love has shown. But whoever has been forgiven little loves little."},{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Your sins are forgiven. Your faith has saved you; go in peace."}],"lesson":{"title":"Forgiven much, love much","text":"Simon thought he was better than the woman, so he didn't think he needed much forgiveness, and he showed Jesus little love. She knew how much she'd been forgiven, so she poured out her love. Leaders remember how much God has forgiven them, and that makes them loving, not judgemental."},"order":["Simon the Pharisee invites Jesus","A sinful woman comes with perfume","She weeps on His feet","Simon judges her","Jesus tells a story of two debts","\"Your sins are forgiven; go in peace\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the woman wipe Jesus' feet with?","o":["Her hair","A towel","Her cloak","Leaves"],"why":"Luke 7:38."},{"q":"In Jesus' story, who would love the moneylender more?","o":["The one forgiven the bigger debt","The one forgiven less","Neither","Both the same"],"why":"Luke 7:43."},{"q":"What did Jesus say to the woman?","o":["Your sins are forgiven; go in peace","Go away","Why are you here?","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 7:48-50."}],"words":["TEARS","PERFUME","FORGIVEN","LOVE","SIMON","PEACE"]},"lk13":{"passage":[[8,1,3]],"intro":[{"sc":"galilee","n":"After this, Jesus travelled from one town and village to another, proclaiming the good news of the kingdom of God. The twelve were with Him."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"But Luke tells us something the other Gospels mostly don't: there were also some women travelling with Jesus."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"Mary called Magdalene, from whom Jesus had driven out seven demons. Joanna, the wife of Chuza, the manager of King Herod's household. Susanna. And many others."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"And these women were helping to support Jesus and the disciples out of their own money!"},{"sc":"galilee","n":"🔎 Did you know? In those days, women were often not allowed to learn from religious teachers, and their word didn't count in court. But Jesus welcomed women as disciples. And it was women who stayed at the cross, and women who were the first witnesses of the resurrection. Joanna is named there too (Luke 24:10)."}],"lesson":{"title":"Hidden supporters matter","text":"Jesus' ministry didn't just run on miracles; it ran on the generosity of women who gave their own money. Their names are only mentioned once or twice, but without them, the mission couldn't have happened. Leaders value the people behind the scenes, and use what they have to support God's work."},"order":["Jesus travels from town to town","The twelve are with Him","Women travel with Him too","Mary Magdalene, Joanna and Susanna","Joanna's husband works for Herod","They support Jesus with their own money"],"quiz":[{"q":"Whose household did Joanna's husband manage?","o":["King Herod's","Pilate's","Caesar's","The high priest's"],"why":"Luke 8:3."},{"q":"How did these women help Jesus?","o":["With their own money","By fighting","By building","By fishing"],"why":"Luke 8:3."},{"q":"Where else is Joanna mentioned?","o":["At the empty tomb","At Jesus' birth","On the boat","Nowhere"],"why":"Luke 24:10."}],"words":["JOANNA","SUSANNA","MARY","SUPPORT","WOMEN","GIVE"]},"lk14":{"passage":[[10,25,37]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","w":"blawyer","e":"smirk","t":"Teacher, what must I do to inherit eternal life?"},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"What is written in the Law?"},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"blawyer","e":"smile","t":"'Love the Lord your God with all your heart, soul, strength and mind,' and 'Love your neighbour as yourself.' ...But who is my neighbour?"},{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"Jesus told a story: \"A man was going down the road from Jerusalem to Jericho, when robbers attacked him. They stripped him, beat him, and went away, leaving him half dead.\""},{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"\"A priest happened to be going down the same road. When he saw the man, he passed by on the other side. So too a Levite, a temple worker. He looked, and passed by on the other side.\""},{"sc":"jerichoroad","w":"bsamaritan","e":"worried","t":"Oh, my friend! Let me help you."},{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"\"But a Samaritan, as he travelled, came where the man was, and when he saw him, he took pity on him. He bandaged his wounds, pouring on oil and wine. Then he put him on his own donkey, brought him to an inn, took care of him, and paid the innkeeper: 'Look after him, and when I return, I'll pay any extra.'\""},{"sc":"jerichoroad","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Which of these three was a neighbour to the man? ...Go and do likewise."},{"sc":"jerichoroad","n":"🔎 Did you know? Jews and Samaritans hated each other! Samaritans were considered outsiders and enemies. Jesus made the 'enemy' the hero of the story. The road from Jerusalem to Jericho really was dangerous: steep, rocky, and famous for robbers."}],"lesson":{"title":"Be a neighbour","text":"The lawyer wanted to know who counted as his neighbour. Jesus turned the question around: don't ask who your neighbour is; BE a neighbour to anyone in need, even someone from a group you don't like. Leaders stop for people others pass by."},"order":["A lawyer asks, \"Who is my neighbour?\"","A man is beaten by robbers","A priest passes by","A Levite passes by","A Samaritan stops and helps","\"Go and do likewise\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who stopped to help the man?","o":["A Samaritan","A priest","A Levite","A soldier"],"why":"Luke 10:33."},{"q":"What did the Samaritan pour on the wounds?","o":["Oil and wine","Water","Honey","Milk"],"why":"Luke 10:34."},{"q":"What did Jesus tell the lawyer to do?","o":["Go and do likewise","Go home","Study more","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 10:37."}],"words":["SAMARITAN","NEIGHBOUR","ROBBERS","ROAD","PITY","HELP"]},"lk15":{"passage":[[10,38,42]],"intro":[{"sc":"kitchen","n":"As Jesus and His disciples travelled, they came to a village where a woman named Martha opened her home to them."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"She had a sister called Mary, who sat at the Lord's feet, listening to what He said."},{"sc":"kitchen","n":"But Martha was distracted by all the preparations that had to be made: cooking, cleaning, serving a big group of hungry guests!"},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"bmartha","e":"frown","t":"Lord, don't You care that my sister has left me to do all the work by myself? Tell her to help me!"},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Martha, Martha, you are worried and upset about many things. But few things are needed, or indeed only one."},{"sc":"kitchen","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Mary has chosen what is better, and it will not be taken away from her."}],"lesson":{"title":"Busy, or close?","text":"Martha's work was good; someone had to cook! But she was so busy serving Jesus that she had no time to listen to Him, and she got upset. Mary chose the 'one thing': sitting with Jesus. Leaders work hard, but make time to sit at Jesus' feet first."},"order":["Martha welcomes Jesus into her home","Mary sits at Jesus' feet","Martha is busy with preparations","\"Tell my sister to help me!\"","\"Martha, you are worried about many things\"","\"Mary has chosen what is better\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What was Mary doing?","o":["Sitting at Jesus' feet, listening","Cooking","Cleaning","Sleeping"],"why":"Luke 10:39."},{"q":"Why was Martha upset?","o":["She was doing all the work alone","She was sick","She lost something","Jesus was late"],"why":"Luke 10:40."},{"q":"What did Jesus say Mary had chosen?","o":["What is better","The wrong thing","To be lazy","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 10:42."}],"words":["MARTHA","MARY","LISTEN","BUSY","WORRIED","BETTER"]},"lk16":{"passage":[[11,5,13]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"One day Jesus was praying. When He finished, one of His disciples said, \"Lord, teach us to pray.\" Jesus taught them the Lord's Prayer, and then told a story."},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Suppose you have a friend, and you go to him at midnight and say, 'Friend, lend me three loaves of bread. A friend of mine on a journey has just arrived, and I have nothing to give him!'"},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"And suppose the one inside answers, 'Don't bother me. The door is already locked, and my children and I are in bed. I can't get up!'"},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"I tell you, even though he won't get up because he's a friend, he WILL get up and give you as much as you need, because you keep on knocking and won't give up!"},{"sc":"townnight","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"So I say to you: Ask and it will be given to you; seek and you will find; knock and the door will be opened. Which of you fathers, if your son asks for a fish, will give him a snake instead? If you know how to give good gifts to your children, how much more will your Father in heaven give the Holy Spirit to those who ask Him!"}],"lesson":{"title":"Keep knocking","text":"If even a grumpy neighbour will get up at midnight because you keep knocking, how much more will your loving Father answer when you pray! Jesus says: keep asking, keep seeking, keep knocking. Leaders pray boldly and persistently, trusting their Father's good heart."},"order":["A disciple asks, \"Teach us to pray\"","A friend knocks at midnight","\"Lend me three loaves\"","\"Don't bother me, I'm in bed!\"","He gets up because the friend keeps knocking","\"Ask, seek, knock\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the friend ask for at midnight?","o":["Three loaves of bread","A lamp","Money","A bed"],"why":"Luke 11:5."},{"q":"Why did the neighbour finally get up?","o":["Because his friend kept on knocking","Because he was hungry","Because of the noise","He didn't"],"why":"Luke 11:8."},{"q":"What will the Father give to those who ask?","o":["The Holy Spirit","Snakes","Stones","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 11:13."}],"words":["KNOCK","MIDNIGHT","ASK","SEEK","FRIEND","BREAD"]},"lk17":{"passage":[[12,13,21]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"Someone in the crowd said, \"Teacher, tell my brother to divide the inheritance with me!\" Jesus said, \"Watch out! Be on your guard against all kinds of greed. Life does not consist in an abundance of possessions.\" Then He told a story."},{"sc":"barns","n":"\"The ground of a certain rich man produced a huge crop. He thought to himself, 'What shall I do? I have no place to store my crops.'\""},{"sc":"barns","w":"brichfool","e":"smile","t":"This is what I'll do! I'll tear down my barns and build bigger ones, and store all my grain. Then I'll say to myself, 'You have plenty of good things laid up for many years. Take life easy; eat, drink and be merry!'"},{"sc":"barns","n":"\"But God said to him, 'You fool! This very night your life will be demanded from you. Then who will get what you have prepared for yourself?'\""},{"sc":"barns","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"This is how it will be with whoever stores up things for themselves but is not rich towards God."},{"sc":"barns","n":"🔎 Did you know? Notice how many times the rich man says 'I', 'my' and 'myself' in just a few sentences: 'MY crops, I will tear down MY barns, I will store MY grain, I'll say to MYSELF...' He never thought about God or anyone else."}],"lesson":{"title":"Rich towards God","text":"The rich man wasn't wrong to have a good harvest. His problem was that he thought only about himself: my, my, my. He planned for years ahead but didn't plan for eternity. Leaders are generous with what they have, and invest in what lasts for ever."},"order":["A man asks Jesus about his inheritance","\"Watch out for greed\"","A rich man has a huge harvest","He plans bigger barns","\"Eat, drink and be merry\"","God says, \"You fool! Tonight...\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the rich man plan to build?","o":["Bigger barns","A temple","A boat","A school"],"why":"Luke 12:18."},{"q":"What did God call him?","o":["A fool","Wise","Generous","A king"],"why":"Luke 12:20."},{"q":"What does Jesus say life does not consist of?","o":["An abundance of possessions","Friends","Love","Food"],"why":"Luke 12:15."}],"words":["BARNS","GREED","RICH","FOOL","MYSELF","GOD"]},"lk18":{"passage":[[13,10,17]],"intro":[{"sc":"synagogue","n":"On a Sabbath, Jesus was teaching in one of the synagogues. A woman was there who had been crippled by a spirit for eighteen years. She was bent over and could not straighten up at all."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Eighteen years of looking at the ground! She couldn't see people's faces, or the sky."},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Woman, you are set free from your infirmity."},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"Jesus put His hands on her, and immediately she straightened up and praised God!"},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bpharisee","e":"frown","t":"There are six days for work. So come and be healed on those days, not on the Sabbath!"},{"sc":"synagogue","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"You hypocrites! Doesn't each of you untie your ox or donkey on the Sabbath and lead it out to give it water? Then shouldn't this woman, a daughter of Abraham, kept bound for eighteen long years, be set free on the Sabbath day?"},{"sc":"synagogue","n":"His opponents were humiliated, but the people were delighted with all the wonderful things He was doing."}],"lesson":{"title":"She is a daughter of Abraham","text":"Everyone saw a bent-over woman; maybe they'd stopped noticing her at all. Jesus noticed her, called her forward, and called her 'a daughter of Abraham': someone precious, part of God's family. Leaders see people's true value, and don't let rules stop them from helping."},"order":["A woman has been bent over for eighteen years","She can't straighten up","Jesus calls her forward","\"You are set free\"","She straightens up and praises God","\"She is a daughter of Abraham\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How long had the woman been bent over?","o":["Eighteen years","Eight days","Two years","Forty years"],"why":"Luke 13:11."},{"q":"What did the woman do when healed?","o":["Straightened up and praised God","Ran away","Cried","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 13:13."},{"q":"What did Jesus call her?","o":["A daughter of Abraham","A sinner","A stranger","A servant"],"why":"Luke 13:16."}],"words":["STRAIGHT","EIGHTEEN","FREE","SABBATH","DAUGHTER","PRAISE"]},"lk19":{"passage":[[14,12,24]],"intro":[{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"When you give a lunch or a dinner, don't invite your friends, brothers, relatives or rich neighbours, who can invite you back. Instead, invite the poor, the crippled, the lame and the blind, and you will be blessed. Although they can't repay you, you will be repaid at the resurrection."},{"sc":"banquet","n":"Then Jesus told a story: \"A man was preparing a great banquet and invited many guests. When it was ready, he sent his servant to tell them, 'Come, everything is ready!'\""},{"sc":"banquet","n":"\"But they all began to make excuses. 'I've just bought a field; I must go and see it.' 'I've just bought five pairs of oxen; I'm going to try them out.' 'I've just got married, so I can't come.'\""},{"sc":"market","n":"\"The owner was angry, and told his servant, 'Go out quickly into the streets and alleys of the town and bring in the poor, the crippled, the blind and the lame!' 'Sir, it's done, but there's still room.' 'Go out to the roads and country lanes and make them come in, so my house will be full!'\""},{"sc":"banquet","n":"🔎 Did you know? In Jesus' time, important people only invited people who could invite them back, or make them look good. Jesus' banquet turns that upside down. God's kingdom is a party where everyone is invited, especially those the world leaves out."}],"lesson":{"title":"Invite those who can't repay","text":"The invited guests made silly excuses. So the host filled his house with the poor and left-out, who were thrilled to come. God invites everyone to His feast. Leaders don't just befriend people who can do something for them. They welcome those who can't repay."},"order":["\"Invite the poor and the blind\"","A man prepares a great banquet","The guests make excuses","\"I bought a field... I bought oxen...\"","He invites the poor, crippled and blind","\"There's still room!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"Who did Jesus say to invite to dinner?","o":["The poor, crippled, lame and blind","Only rich friends","Only family","Nobody"],"why":"Luke 14:13."},{"q":"What excuse did one guest give?","o":["\"I've bought five pairs of oxen\"","\"I'm sick\"","\"It's raining\"","\"I'm lost\""],"why":"Luke 14:19."},{"q":"Who came to the banquet in the end?","o":["The poor and left-out from the streets and lanes","Nobody","Only the first guests","Soldiers"],"why":"Luke 14:21-23."}],"words":["BANQUET","INVITE","EXCUSES","POOR","ROOM","FEAST"]},"lk20":{"passage":[[15,1,10]],"intro":[{"sc":"market","n":"Tax collectors and 'sinners' were all gathering around to hear Jesus. But the Pharisees and teachers of the law muttered, \"This man welcomes sinners and eats with them!\" So Jesus told them three stories about lost things."},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Suppose one of you has a hundred sheep and loses one of them. Doesn't he leave the ninety-nine in the open country and go after the lost sheep until he finds it?"},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"And when he finds it, he joyfully puts it on his shoulders and goes home. He calls his friends and neighbours together: 'Rejoice with me; I have found my lost sheep!'"},{"sc":"hut","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Or suppose a woman has ten silver coins and loses one. Doesn't she light a lamp, sweep the house and search carefully until she finds it? And when she finds it, she calls her friends: 'Rejoice with me; I have found my lost coin!'"},{"sc":"field","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"In the same way, I tell you, there is rejoicing in the presence of the angels of God over one sinner who repents."}],"lesson":{"title":"Every single one matters","text":"One sheep out of a hundred, one coin out of ten. Most people would say 'never mind'. But the shepherd and the woman searched until they found it, then threw a party! That's how much God cares about each person. Leaders go looking for the one who's missing, and celebrate when they come back."},"order":["The Pharisees complain about sinners","A shepherd loses one sheep out of a hundred","He searches until he finds it","A woman loses one of ten coins","She sweeps until she finds it","Heaven rejoices over one who repents"],"quiz":[{"q":"How many sheep did the shepherd have?","o":["A hundred","Ten","Twelve","A thousand"],"why":"Luke 15:4."},{"q":"What did the woman do to find her coin?","o":["Lit a lamp and swept the house","Gave up","Bought a new one","Asked a neighbour"],"why":"Luke 15:8."},{"q":"Who rejoices over one sinner who repents?","o":["The angels of God","Nobody","Only the Pharisees","The coin"],"why":"Luke 15:10."}],"words":["LOST","SHEEP","COIN","FOUND","REJOICE","SEARCH"]},"lk21":{"passage":[[15,11,24]],"intro":[{"sc":"tents","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"There was a man who had two sons. The younger one said to his father, 'Father, give me my share of the inheritance now.' (That was like saying, 'I wish you were dead.')"},{"sc":"farcountry","n":"The younger son packed up everything and went off to a distant country, where he wasted all his money on wild living."},{"sc":"farcountry","n":"Then a severe famine hit the country. He had nothing. He took a job feeding pigs, and he was so hungry he wanted to eat the pigs' food, but no one gave him anything."},{"sc":"farcountry","w":"bprodigal","e":"worried","t":"My father's servants have food to spare, and here I am starving! I'll go back to my father and say, 'Father, I have sinned against heaven and against you. I'm no longer worthy to be called your son. Make me like one of your servants.'"},{"sc":"field","n":"\"But while he was still a long way off, his father saw him and was filled with compassion. He RAN to his son, threw his arms around him and kissed him.\""},{"sc":"field","w":"bfatherlk","e":"big","t":"Quick! Bring the best robe and put it on him! Put a ring on his finger and sandals on his feet! Bring the fattened calf. Let's have a feast and celebrate! For this son of mine was dead and is alive again; he was lost and is found!"},{"sc":"field","n":"🔎 Did you know? In that culture, an important old man would never run; it was undignified. But this father ran! The robe, ring and sandals meant: you're not a servant, you're my son. That's how God welcomes us home."}],"lesson":{"title":"The Father runs to you","text":"The son had wasted everything and expected to be a servant at best. But the father was watching for him, ran to him, and threw a party. However far you've wandered, God the Father is watching the road, ready to run to you. Leaders welcome people back the way the Father does."},"order":["The younger son asks for his inheritance","He wastes it in a far country","He ends up feeding pigs","He decides to go home","The father runs to meet him","\"He was lost and is found!\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What job did the younger son end up doing?","o":["Feeding pigs","Fishing","Farming wheat","Building"],"why":"Luke 15:15."},{"q":"What did the father do when he saw his son coming?","o":["Ran to him and hugged him","Waited inside","Shouted at him","Locked the door"],"why":"Luke 15:20."},{"q":"What did the father give his son?","o":["The best robe, a ring and sandals","A job as a servant","Nothing","A lecture"],"why":"Luke 15:22."}],"words":["PRODIGAL","FATHER","RAN","ROBE","RING","HOME"]},"lk22":{"passage":[[15,25,32]],"intro":[{"sc":"field","n":"Meanwhile, the older son was working in the field. When he came near the house, he heard music and dancing! He called a servant: \"What's going on?\" \"Your brother has come home, and your father has killed the fattened calf because he's back safe and sound.\""},{"sc":"field","n":"The older brother became angry and refused to go in. So his father went out and pleaded with him."},{"sc":"field","w":"bolderbro","e":"frown","t":"Look! All these years I've been slaving for you and never disobeyed your orders. Yet you never gave me even a young goat to celebrate with my friends. But when this son of yours, who has wasted your money, comes home, you kill the fattened calf for him!"},{"sc":"field","w":"bfatherlk","e":"smile","t":"My son, you are always with me, and everything I have is yours. But we had to celebrate and be glad, because this brother of yours was dead and is alive again; he was lost and is found."},{"sc":"field","n":"And there the story ends. We never find out if the older brother went in to the party."},{"sc":"field","n":"🔎 Did you know? Jesus told these stories to the Pharisees, who were complaining that He welcomed sinners. The older brother was them! Did they join God's party, or stay outside, angry? Jesus left the story open, for them, and for us, to finish."}],"lesson":{"title":"Don't miss the party","text":"The older brother did everything right on the outside, but his heart was cold and jealous. He called his brother 'this son of yours', not 'my brother'. The father loved him too and went out to plead with him. Leaders celebrate when others are forgiven, instead of feeling jealous."},"order":["The older son hears music","His brother has come home","He refuses to go in","\"I've slaved for you all these years!\"","\"Everything I have is yours\"","\"Your brother was lost and is found\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How did the older brother react?","o":["He was angry and refused to go in","He ran to hug his brother","He danced","He cooked"],"why":"Luke 15:28."},{"q":"Who went out to plead with him?","o":["The father","The younger son","A servant","Nobody"],"why":"Luke 15:28."},{"q":"How does the story end?","o":["We don't know if the older brother went in","He went in happily","He ran away","He hit his brother"],"why":"Luke 15:32."}],"words":["BROTHER","JEALOUS","PARTY","FATHER","CELEBRATE","FOUND"]},"lk23":{"passage":[[16,19,25]],"intro":[{"sc":"banquet","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"There was a rich man who was dressed in purple and fine linen and lived in luxury every day."},{"sc":"citygate","n":"\"At his gate lay a poor man named Lazarus, covered with sores, longing to eat what fell from the rich man's table. Even the dogs came and licked his sores.\" The rich man walked past him every day, and did nothing."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"\"The time came when the poor man died, and the angels carried him to Abraham's side. The rich man also died and was buried.\""},{"sc":"starsky","n":"\"In the place of the dead, where he was in torment, the rich man looked up and saw Abraham far away, with Lazarus by his side. He called out, 'Father Abraham, have pity on me!'\""},{"sc":"starsky","n":"\"But Abraham replied, 'Son, remember that in your lifetime you received your good things, while Lazarus received bad things. But now he is comforted here and you are in agony. And between us a great chasm has been set in place.'\""},{"sc":"citygate","n":"🔎 Did you know? This is the only one of Jesus' stories where a character has a name, and it's the poor man! The rich man has no name. In the world, the rich are famous and the poor are forgotten. In God's eyes, it's the other way round."}],"lesson":{"title":"Notice who's at your gate","text":"The rich man wasn't punished for being rich. He walked past a suffering man at his own gate every single day, and did nothing. Jesus gave the poor man a name and left the rich man nameless. Leaders notice the people at their 'gate', and help."},"order":["A rich man lives in luxury","Poor Lazarus lies at his gate","The rich man does nothing","Both men die","Lazarus is comforted","A great chasm separates them"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Lazarus lie?","o":["At the rich man's gate","In the temple","In a palace","By the lake"],"why":"Luke 16:20."},{"q":"Who is the only named character in this story?","o":["The poor man, Lazarus","The rich man","Abraham only","Nobody"],"why":"Luke 16:20."},{"q":"What was the rich man's real wrong?","o":["He ignored the suffering man at his gate","He was rich","He wore purple","He had a gate"],"why":"Luke 16:19-21."}],"words":["LAZARUS","GATE","RICH","POOR","NOTICE","CHASM"]},"lk24":{"passage":[[17,11,19]],"intro":[{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"On His way to Jerusalem, Jesus travelled along the border between Samaria and Galilee. As He was going into a village, ten men with leprosy met Him. They stood at a distance and called out in a loud voice:"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bleperm","e":"worried","t":"Jesus, Master, have pity on us!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Go, show yourselves to the priests."},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"And as they went, they were cleansed! All ten of them!"},{"sc":"hillcountry","n":"One of them, when he saw he was healed, came back, praising God in a loud voice. He threw himself at Jesus' feet and thanked Him. And he was a Samaritan."},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Weren't all ten cleansed? Where are the other nine? Has no one returned to give praise to God except this foreigner?"},{"sc":"hillcountry","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Rise and go; your faith has made you well."}],"lesson":{"title":"Come back and say thank you","text":"Ten were healed. Only one came back to say thank you, and he was the outsider, the Samaritan. It's easy to receive good things from God and forget to thank Him. Leaders make thankfulness a habit, and say thank you to God and to people."},"order":["Ten men with leprosy call to Jesus","\"Show yourselves to the priests\"","As they go, they are healed","One comes back praising God","He is a Samaritan","\"Where are the other nine?\""],"quiz":[{"q":"How many men were healed?","o":["Ten","One","Nine","Twelve"],"why":"Luke 17:12."},{"q":"How many came back to say thank you?","o":["One","Ten","Nine","None"],"why":"Luke 17:15."},{"q":"Where was the thankful man from?","o":["Samaria","Jerusalem","Rome","Egypt"],"why":"Luke 17:16."}],"words":["TEN","THANKFUL","LEPERS","SAMARITAN","HEALED","PRAISE"]},"lk25":{"passage":[[18,9,14]],"intro":[{"sc":"temple","n":"Jesus told this story to some people who were confident of their own goodness and looked down on everyone else."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Two men went up to the temple to pray. One was a Pharisee and the other a tax collector."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bpharisee","e":"smirk","t":"God, I thank You that I am not like other people: robbers, evildoers, or even like this tax collector! I fast twice a week and give a tenth of all I get."},{"sc":"temple","n":"The Pharisee stood up proudly, and 'prayed about himself'. He wasn't really talking to God at all; he was showing off."},{"sc":"temple","w":"btaxman","e":"worried","t":"God, have mercy on me, a sinner."},{"sc":"temple","n":"The tax collector stood at a distance. He wouldn't even look up to heaven, but beat his chest in sorrow."},{"sc":"temple","w":"bjesus","e":"stern","t":"I tell you that this man, rather than the other, went home justified before God. For all those who exalt themselves will be humbled, and those who humble themselves will be exalted."}],"lesson":{"title":"Humble hearts","text":"The Pharisee's prayer was all about himself, and he looked down on others. The tax collector's prayer was seven words long, and honest: 'God, have mercy on me, a sinner.' God heard the humble one. Leaders pray honestly and humbly, and never look down on others."},"order":["Two men go to the temple to pray","The Pharisee boasts about himself","He looks down on the tax collector","The tax collector won't look up","\"God, have mercy on me, a sinner\"","The humble man goes home justified"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did the Pharisee thank God for?","o":["That he wasn't like other people","For forgiveness","For his family","For food"],"why":"Luke 18:11."},{"q":"What did the tax collector pray?","o":["God, have mercy on me, a sinner","Thank You I'm good","Make me rich","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 18:13."},{"q":"Who went home right with God?","o":["The tax collector","The Pharisee","Both","Neither"],"why":"Luke 18:14."}],"words":["PRAYER","HUMBLE","MERCY","PROUD","SINNER","TEMPLE"]},"lk26":{"passage":[[19,1,10]],"intro":[{"sc":"sycamore","n":"Jesus entered Jericho and was passing through. A man was there named Zacchaeus. He was a chief tax collector, and very rich, mostly from cheating people."},{"sc":"sycamore","n":"He wanted to see who Jesus was, but because he was short, he couldn't see over the crowd. And nobody would let him through!"},{"sc":"sycamore","n":"So he ran ahead and climbed a sycamore-fig tree to see Him, since Jesus was coming that way."},{"sc":"sycamore","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Zacchaeus, come down immediately. I must stay at your house today!"},{"sc":"sycamore","n":"He came down at once and welcomed Him gladly. But all the people saw this and began to mutter, \"He has gone to be the guest of a sinner!\""},{"sc":"sycamore","w":"bzacchaeus","e":"big","t":"Look, Lord! Here and now I give half of my possessions to the poor, and if I have cheated anybody out of anything, I will pay back four times the amount!"},{"sc":"sycamore","w":"bjesus","e":"big","t":"Today salvation has come to this house. For the Son of Man came to seek and to save the lost."}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus knows your name","text":"Everyone hated Zacchaeus. But Jesus stopped under his tree, called him by name, and invited Himself to his house! That kindness changed Zacchaeus completely: he gave back far more than he'd taken. Leaders show kindness to people others reject. It can change everything."},"order":["Zacchaeus is a rich chief tax collector","He's too short to see Jesus","He climbs a sycamore-fig tree","Jesus calls him by name","\"I must stay at your house today!\"","Zacchaeus gives half to the poor"],"quiz":[{"q":"Why did Zacchaeus climb a tree?","o":["He was too short to see over the crowd","To hide","To pick figs","For fun"],"why":"Luke 19:3-4."},{"q":"How much did Zacchaeus promise to pay back?","o":["Four times the amount","Half","Nothing","Double"],"why":"Luke 19:8."},{"q":"What did Jesus say He came to do?","o":["Seek and save the lost","Collect taxes","Climb trees","Rule Jericho"],"why":"Luke 19:10."}],"words":["ZACCHAEUS","TREE","SHORT","SYCAMORE","SALVATION","LOST"]},"lk27":{"passage":[[23,32,43]],"intro":[{"sc":"golgotha","n":"Two other men, both criminals, were led out with Jesus to be executed. When they came to the place called the Skull, they crucified Him there, with the criminals, one on His right and one on His left."},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bjesus","e":"worried","t":"Father, forgive them, for they do not know what they are doing."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"The people stood watching. The rulers sneered. The soldiers mocked Him. One of the criminals hanging there hurled insults: \"Aren't You the Messiah? Save Yourself and us!\""},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bthief","e":"stern","t":"Don't you fear God? We're punished justly, for we're getting what our deeds deserve. But this man has done nothing wrong."},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bthief","e":"worried","t":"Jesus, remember me when You come into Your kingdom."},{"sc":"golgotha","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Truly I tell you, today you will be with Me in paradise."},{"sc":"golgotha","n":"Darkness came over the whole land. Then Jesus called out with a loud voice, \"Father, into Your hands I commit My spirit.\" And He breathed His last."}],"lesson":{"title":"It's never too late","text":"The criminal had nothing to offer: no good deeds, no time left, no way to make up for his life. All he could do was ask Jesus to remember him. And Jesus promised him paradise, that very day. Salvation is a gift, never earned. And even dying, Jesus prayed for His enemies."},"order":["Jesus is crucified between two criminals","\"Father, forgive them\"","One criminal mocks Jesus","The other says, \"This man has done nothing wrong\"","\"Jesus, remember me\"","\"Today you will be with Me in paradise\""],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus pray for those crucifying Him?","o":["Father, forgive them","Punish them","Help Me","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 23:34."},{"q":"What did the second criminal ask?","o":["Jesus, remember me when You come into Your kingdom","Save us!","Get us down!","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 23:42."},{"q":"What did Jesus promise him?","o":["Today you will be with Me in paradise","Maybe one day","No","Ask God"],"why":"Luke 23:43."}],"words":["PARADISE","FORGIVE","REMEMBER","TODAY","CROSS","GRACE"]},"lk28":{"passage":[[24,13,35]],"intro":[{"sc":"emmaus","n":"That same Sunday, two of Jesus' followers were walking to a village called Emmaus, about eleven kilometres from Jerusalem. They were talking about everything that had happened."},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"Jesus Himself came up and walked along with them, but they were kept from recognising Him. \"What are you discussing as you walk along?\" They stood still, their faces downcast."},{"sc":"emmaus","w":"bcleopas","e":"worried","t":"Are You the only visitor to Jerusalem who doesn't know what's happened? Jesus of Nazareth was a prophet, powerful in word and deed. But our leaders handed Him over to be crucified. We had hoped He was the one who would redeem Israel. And some women amazed us this morning: they said the tomb was empty!"},{"sc":"emmaus","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"How foolish you are, and how slow to believe all that the prophets have spoken! Didn't the Messiah have to suffer these things and then enter His glory?"},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"And beginning with Moses and all the Prophets, He explained to them what was said in all the Scriptures about Himself. When they reached the village, they urged Him, \"Stay with us; it's nearly evening.\""},{"sc":"lastsupper","n":"At the table, He took bread, gave thanks, broke it and began to give it to them. Then their eyes were opened, and they recognised Him! And He disappeared from their sight."},{"sc":"lastsupper","w":"bcleopas","e":"big","t":"Weren't our hearts burning within us while He talked with us on the road and opened the Scriptures to us?"},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"They got up at once and ran back to Jerusalem, eleven kilometres in the dark, to tell the others: \"It's true! The Lord has risen!\""}],"lesson":{"title":"Jesus in all the Scriptures","text":"Jesus' Bible study on the Emmaus road went from Moses through all the prophets, showing them Himself everywhere. That's exactly what the 'Pointing to Jesus' and 'Promise kept' slides in this game are for! Leaders read the whole Bible looking for Jesus, and their hearts burn."},"order":["Two followers walk to Emmaus, sad","Jesus walks with them, unrecognised","\"We had hoped He was the one\"","He explains the Scriptures about Himself","He breaks bread, and they recognise Him","They run back to Jerusalem"],"quiz":[{"q":"Where were the two followers walking?","o":["Emmaus","Bethlehem","Nazareth","Galilee"],"why":"Luke 24:13."},{"q":"When did they recognise Jesus?","o":["When He broke the bread","Straight away","Never","When He said His name"],"why":"Luke 24:30-31."},{"q":"What did they say about their hearts?","o":["They were burning within them","They were broken","They were cold","Nothing"],"why":"Luke 24:32."}],"words":["EMMAUS","ROAD","HEARTS","BURNING","BREAD","SCRIPTURES"]},"lk29":{"passage":[[24,36,53]],"intro":[{"sc":"upperroom","n":"While the disciples were still talking, Jesus Himself stood among them. \"Peace be with you.\" They were startled and frightened, thinking they'd seen a ghost."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"Why are you troubled? Look at My hands and My feet. It is I Myself! Touch Me and see; a ghost doesn't have flesh and bones, as you see I have."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"They still couldn't believe it for joy! So He asked, \"Do you have anything here to eat?\" They gave Him a piece of broiled fish, and He took it and ate it in front of them!"},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"bjesus","e":"smile","t":"This is what is written: the Messiah will suffer and rise from the dead on the third day, and repentance for the forgiveness of sins will be preached in His name to all nations, beginning at Jerusalem. You are witnesses of these things. Stay in the city until you have been clothed with power from on high."},{"sc":"ascension","n":"He led them out to the vicinity of Bethany, lifted up His hands and blessed them. While He was blessing them, He left them and was taken up into heaven."},{"sc":"temple","n":"Then they worshipped Him and returned to Jerusalem with great joy. And they stayed continually at the temple, praising God."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"🔎 Did you know? Why did Jesus eat fish? To prove He wasn't a ghost! His resurrection body was real, with scars on His hands and feet, and He could eat. Luke the doctor wanted readers to know this really happened."}],"lesson":{"title":"Witnesses with great joy","text":"Jesus proved He was really alive: touch Me, watch Me eat! Then He blessed them, and was taken up into heaven, and they went back full of great joy, not sadness. He called them 'witnesses'. Leaders who know Jesus is alive become joyful witnesses to everyone."},"order":["Jesus appears among the disciples","\"Touch Me and see\"","He eats a piece of fish","\"You are witnesses\"","He blesses them at Bethany","He is taken up into heaven"],"quiz":[{"q":"What did Jesus eat to prove He wasn't a ghost?","o":["Broiled fish","Bread","Grapes","Honey"],"why":"Luke 24:42-43."},{"q":"What was Jesus doing when He was taken up into heaven?","o":["Blessing them","Sleeping","Eating","Walking away"],"why":"Luke 24:51."},{"q":"How did the disciples feel afterwards?","o":["Great joy","Very sad","Afraid","Angry"],"why":"Luke 24:52."}],"words":["ASCENSION","WITNESSES","BLESSED","JOY","HANDS","HEAVEN"]}});
